# .NET build output.
#
# FogApi/bin is a build artifact even though it sits inside the module payload.
# The dll has to be next to the manifest that names it in RequiredAssemblies,
# because three things import straight out of the source tree: build.ps1, CI's
# settings bootstrap check, and every Tests/*.Tests.ps1 BeforeAll.
#
# Without this entry, tag-and-release.yml's `git add -A` commits a dll to
# master on every release. The generated .cs under src/ IS committed -- that is
# the reviewable artifact, the same rule the generated .ps1 files follow.
FogApi/bin/
src/*/bin/
src/*/obj/

# Throwaway spike modules.
.spike/

# AutoRest output is NOT committed -- the opposite of the src/ rule above, and a
# deliberate reversal rather than an inherited default.
#
# Why: a run emits ~2,570 files, ~1,460 of them models, four per model. A diff
# that size is not read by anyone, so committing it buys the appearance of
# reviewability without the substance.
#
# What it costs: the public surface becomes invisible in a PR. A regeneration
# can rename, add or drop a cmdlet and nobody sees it until release. That is
# paid for by the committed surface snapshot -- see
# spec/generators/Invoke-FogApiGeneration.ps1 and the surface-diff CI gate. If
# the snapshot ever stops being trustworthy, DELETE THIS BLOCK and commit the
# output instead; nothing else depends on the choice.
#
# NOTE FOR WHOEVER PORTS THE HELPERS: src/custom/ is the one directory in the
# scaffold that AutoRest intends to be hand-edited, and it is the planned home
# for Invoke-FogApi.cs and the workflow helpers. Two things have to change
# before anything is written there, and both are easy to miss:
#
#   1. Narrow this ignore, or hand-written code will never be committed:
#        FogApi-clients/pwsh/src/*
#        !FogApi-clients/pwsh/src/custom/
#
#   2. Invoke-FogApiGeneration.ps1 passes --clear-output-folder, which empties
#      the output folder before generating. Verify it spares custom/ before
#      trusting it with source that exists nowhere else. It is there because
#      the surface is not committed and a stale generated file would otherwise
#      ship as though it had been generated.
#
# Ignoring the whole directory is correct only while src/ is entirely
# generated, which it is today.
FogApi-clients/pwsh/src/

# The scaffold's former home, kept ignored on purpose. Moving the output path
# without this line un-ignored a stale generation and staged 489 files and
# 89,374 insertions of generated code in one commit -- the exact thing the
# block above exists to prevent. Anyone passing -OutputFolder by hand can land
# here again.
spec/generators/out/
